WEBVTT

00:03.810 --> 00:06.690
5 Centimeters per Second

00:07.650 --> 00:09.530
Story One{ending reads, "a chain of short stories". So I'm going with "Story" which can be a translation of 話. Official subs go with the usual "Episode"}

00:11.120 --> 00:12.080
Hey...

00:12.490 --> 00:14.870
They say it's five centimeters per second.

00:14.870 --> 00:16.410
Huh? What is?

00:16.660 --> 00:21.040
The speed at which cherry blossoms fall.
It's five centimeters per second.

00:22.750 --> 00:25.340
You sure know a lot of stuff like that, Akari.

00:27.590 --> 00:31.800
Say... don't you think it kinda looks like snow?

00:31.800 --> 00:33.260
I guess...

00:36.220 --> 00:38.480
Hey! Wait up!

00:45.280 --> 00:46.110
Akari!

00:46.150 --> 00:46.990
Takaki-kun!

00:49.740 --> 00:53.740
It'd be great if we could watch the cherry
blossoms fall again together next year.

00:56.160 --> 01:09.460
Cherry Blossom

01:07.210 --> 01:08.630
"To Thono Takaki-sama."

01:09.090 --> 01:11.260
"It's been a really long time."

01:16.310 --> 01:21.850
"Summer's pretty hot around here,
but compared to Tokyo, it's so much milder."

01:22.350 --> 01:27.900
"But when I think about it,
I liked Tokyo's hot, humid summers, too."

01:28.150 --> 01:30.530
"The melting-hot asphalt,"

01:30.700 --> 01:32.950
"the distant skyscrapers, shimmering in the heat,"

01:32.950 --> 01:36.450
"and the freezing air-conditioning
in department stores and on subways."

01:36.830 --> 01:41.330
"The last time we were together was at
our elementary school graduation."

01:41.540 --> 01:43.330
"It's already been half a year since."

01:44.290 --> 01:46.170
"So, Takaki-kun..."

01:46.880 --> 01:49.880
"...do you still remember me?."

01:53.890 --> 01:56.220
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

01:55.050 --> 01:56.670
S{*\c&H2D251D&}t{*\c&H2C241C&}ud{*\c&H2B231B&}e{*\c&H2B231A&}nt {*\c&H292118&}C{*\c&H292117&}ou{*\c&H282016&}nc{*\c&H271F15&}il {*\c&H261E14&}Room

01:56.680 --> 01:57.930
"Thanks for replying."

01:57.970 --> 01:59.520
"It made me so happy."

02:00.430 --> 02:04.730
"It's already well into autumn and the
leaves are turning beautiful colors."

02:05.150 --> 02:09.400
"I had to pull out a sweater the day before
yesterday for the first time this year."

02:10.150 --> 02:10.990
Tohno-kun.

02:11.030 --> 02:12.030
Senpai.

02:12.490 --> 02:14.030
What's that? A love letter?

02:14.320 --> 02:15.240
That's not it.

02:15.280 --> 02:17.080
Sorry for having asked you to do all that.

02:17.080 --> 02:18.450
No problem, I finished quickly.

02:18.450 --> 02:21.160
Thanks. So, is it true that you'll be transferring schools?

02:21.160 --> 02:23.370
Ah, yes, at the end of the year.

02:23.460 --> 02:24.290
Where to?

02:24.370 --> 02:26.750
Kagoshima. Because of my parents.

02:26.750 --> 02:28.750
I see... it'll be lonely around here without you.

02:28.750 --> 02:34.300
"I'm actually writing this letter on the train because
practice has been starting really early lately."

02:34.430 --> 02:36.590
"I had my hair cut the other day."

02:36.800 --> 02:39.010
"It's so short you can even see my ears..."

02:39.510 --> 02:43.350
"...so you probably wouldn't 
even recognize me if you saw me."

02:43.560 --> 02:44.140
I'm back.

02:44.310 --> 02:45.190
Welcome home.

02:50.770 --> 02:55.320
Dear Shinohara Akari-sama

02:54.240 --> 02:58.990
"I bet you're changing little by little too, Takaki-kun."

03:13.550 --> 03:14.720
"Dear Takaki-kun..."

03:14.970 --> 03:18.390
"Have you been doing well during these cold days?"

03:23.220 --> 03:25.810
"It's already snowed a number of times here."

03:25.980 --> 03:30.270
"Every time it does, I wrap myself
 in layers of clothes when I go to school."

03:30.940 --> 03:33.860
"It hasn't snowed in Tokyo yet, right?."

03:33.860 --> 03:36.150
"Even though I moved away..."

03:36.150 --> 03:39.490
"...I still look at Tokyo's weather forecast out of habit."

03:43.790 --> 03:45.620
Wish it would rain one of these days...

03:45.620 --> 03:47.620
It wouldn't be any better indoors.

03:47.870 --> 03:51.090
Say... have you guys ever been to Tochigi?

03:51.090 --> 03:52.210
Huh? Where?

03:52.420 --> 03:53.000
Tochigi.

03:53.210 --> 03:53.880
Nope.

03:54.510 --> 03:55.720
I wonder how you get there...

03:56.130 --> 03:56.880
No clue.

03:57.050 --> 03:58.800
A bullet train or something?

03:59.220 --> 04:00.220
It's a long way...

04:02.680 --> 04:03.510
Freshmen!

04:03.560 --> 04:04.140
Yes?!

04:05.220 --> 04:08.440
Onto the final three laps! Fight! Fight!

04:08.440 --> 04:13.320
"I was surprised to hear that you were
the one transferring schools this time."

